WEBVTT

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.740
Hop, step, jump.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.640
Drew, draw, drawn.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.450
Chip, syrup, whip.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.900
Who I wanna be. {naritai atashi}

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.150
They call me calm, strong, and cool. {cool de tsuyoku...}

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:40.500
Everyone says I'm popular.{iketeru to...}

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.910
But the truth is, I'm not like that at all. {honto wa...}

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.120
I'm just an ordinary girl! {futsuu ni...}

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.230
I wish I could just get rid {puressha nank...}

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:55.010
of all this pressure and be myself. {sunao ni naritai...}

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:58.850
But they'd all say it's out of character. {kyarajanai toka...}

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:03.260
Unlock my heart! {atashi no kokoro...}

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:08.610
Just be who you wanna be. {naritai...}

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:11.460
Your Guardian Characters are with you. {shugo kyara ga...}

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.710
Just do it the way you wanna do it. {yaritai...}

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:18.780
It'll be okay, really! {zenzen...}

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:23.690
Just be who you wanna be. {naritai...}

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:26.460
Having only one style would be way too boring. {hitotsu...}

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:30.720
Just do it the way you wanna do it. {yaritai...}

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.990
You can do anything! {nandatte...}

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:36.610
I know that...{kitto}

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.450
Hop, step, jump.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:40.340
Drew, draw, drawn.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.210
Chip, syrup, whip.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.520
...is who I wanna be. {naritai atashi}

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:51.830
Look, look, Amu-chi!

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.480
I got a fan of Sho-kun from DARTS!

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:57.230
I got a Kagawa Masashi-sama hand towel.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:59.280
Uh, that's good.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:02.510
Hey, hey, do you have any favorite singers, Amu-chi?

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:05.470
Hm, let me think. Huh?

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:09.550
Hoshina Utau?

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:12.340
She became the singing queen all of a sudden, didn't she?

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:18.150
Since she works for Easter, does that mean she's an enemy, too?

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:24.540
A Gift For You!

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:24.540
Episode 20

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.600
Hey, hey, where are we going next? What'll we buy?

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:30.330
Aren't you already over your budget for today?

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.010
It's okay!

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:35.020
Huh? Kukai?

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:37.090
He would appear to be eat-

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:38.220
Hamburgers!

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:41.360
I want one, too!

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.940
Really? That's incredible.  {This is spoken by the man at the counter at ~2:48}

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.670
Wow, what a great place. {lit: has a good feeling}

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:55.470
It's the type of place you'd see in an American movie.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.350
But it really doesn't suit Kukai.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:01.750
You can say that, but I've been coming here since I was a kid.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:02.960
Welcome!

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:09.280
Kukai's grown so big by eating the hamburgers here, instead of drinking milk.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:10.070
Shion.

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:13.470
Bringing three girls with you, what a stud!

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.260
They're friends from school.

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:18.000
She's Shion. I've known her since I was a kid.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.190
Nice to meet you.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:22.540
So you've known Soma-kun since he was small?

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:24.160
Yep, since he was born.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:28.350
Oh, oh! What was he like when he was little?

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:30.050
Let's see...

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:33.120
He was the type who'd laugh like nothing was wrong even if he peed his pants.

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:33.860
What?

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:34.820
Really?

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:36.470
That's so like him!

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:39.240
I don't remember that at all!

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:41.960
So which of them are you serious about?

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:42.560
Huh?

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:45.640
Don't try to hide it. Tell me.

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:48.320
Shion, I give! I give!

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:48.700
Tell me!

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.470
Hey, Shion, do that thing you always do.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:52.640
No.

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:54.730
I'm busy serving customers right now.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.790
But she was just goofing off.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:59.580
It's okay, Shion-chan, they can all wait.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.050
Right on, Boss! {Or something like "That's the way, master". I always have trouble with "sasuga"}

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:02.500
Shion-chan, please!

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:03.590
Please!

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.360
If you insist.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:10.520
What's about to happen?

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:11.870
Something good.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:13.850
Oh...

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:15.960
A piano.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:24.680
It's jazz!

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:38.340
With a light and springy touch, the sound dances!

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:40.340
Let's dance, too! {This should be at ~4:38 starting with "orotachi"}

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:41.980
Okay!

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:44.240
Yahoo!

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:47.730
Yeah!

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:07.720
That's my Shion!

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:08.740
Incredible!

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:10.930
It was great! The best! {etc}

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.630
How is it? Like Shion-chan?

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:18.960
Not at all.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.650
It sounds like you're trying to get rid of some stress.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:25.840
Hey, guys. Why are we meeting in the music room?

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:28.530
Yuiki-san insisted.

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:30.970
She wanted to act like Shion.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:34.890
Shion-san looked so cool playing the piano, so I wanted to play, too.

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:40.300
I had no idea you had such a wonderful acquaintance, Soma-kun.

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:45.220
My house is close to hers, and she's friends with my parents, so she's like my big sister.

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:47.380
By the way, how old is she?

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:51.440
She'll be 19 soon. I think her birthday's next week.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.570
It's a chance! A big chance!

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:54.490
For what?

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:56.860
For a childhood friend to be reborn as a girlfriend!

00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:57.220
What?

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:59.740
A birthday is the perfect event for that!

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:02.930
Girlfriend... Wait, Kukai and Shion-san?

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:04.030
Naturally!

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:05.360
Huh? What're you talking about?

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:08.080
Right, their ages are too far apart!

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:12.690
Tsk tsk tsk, Amu-chi, you don't get it. In love, an age difference...

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:14.050
...doesn't matter!

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:17.560
I didn't know!

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:19.980
Jeez, weren't you guys listening?

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:21.780
Shion and I are like siblings!

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:22.620
That just gives you the opportunity...

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:23.800
...to change the relationship!

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:27.590
If I can do anything, let me know.

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:29.620
I'd be happy to help.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:32.100
Gotta love that airheadedness. {lit: naturalness, though since "tennen" is a sort of generic prefix, I've decided that he was using it as short for "tennenboke", which is a natural airhead.}

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:42.400
I know we have no customers, but I think you're slacking off a little too much.

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:47.120
When I think that I might not be able to hear you play anymore, I get so sad.

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:53.340
Boss. Jeez, don't say stuff like that!

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:57.550
Though, I do feel a little uneasy about this, too. {lit: pre-trip uneasy feeling}

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:01.630
Sorry, sorry. I'm rooting for you, so do your best.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:04.790
I will.

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:10.360
Man, I'll be caught up in their plans for a little while.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:11.770
For you and Shion?

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:15.670
Yeah. But if I tell her, I think she'll play along.

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:25.500
Shion!

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:46.380
Nailed it!

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.530
What are you doing?

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:53.620
Looking for a four-leaf clover. I thought I might find one here.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.780
Why are you looking for something like that?

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:58.580
For a good luck charm.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:00.490
You still believe in that?

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:04.030
You used to believe in it, too!

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:06.490
It's okay to believe in stuff like this forever!

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:07.700
Really?

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:10.060
You're not very cute lately.

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:21.310
We haven't been here together in a while.

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:23.220
Yeah.

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:29.910
Kukai, I'm... I'm going to leave this city soon.

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:30.930
What?

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:36.260
I'll be going to a music school where a pianist I respect is an instructor.

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:40.450
I want to find out how far my sound will take me. {lit: find out how far my sound will be accepted}

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:41.820
That's great!

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:44.260
It's always been your dream to play the piano.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:48.290
Don't just say it straight out, it's embarrassing.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:49.760
But it's true, right? {lit: It has been, right?}

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:51.480
Well, yeah.

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:54.450
Your piano playing will take you as far as you want to go.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:59.540
It's not that simple. There are lots of people who can play like I do.

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:01.050
It'll be fine.

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:06.260
I love listening to you play.

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:10.580
What?

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:14.010
What do you mean by "what?" I'm just telling the truth.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.270
All right, just be quiet.

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:18.190
What's with you? Jeez.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:21.670
I can't find one.

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:25.320
Don't give up. Let me help you.

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:30.290
Well then, I'll leave it to you.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:31.770
Don't go to sleep!

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:36.180
Hey! Wake up, Shion!

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:38.380
No, I can't eat any more.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:40.290
That's so unoriginal!

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:49.840
Camera batteries successfully acquired! The errand for Dad is complete! {sounds very military}

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:53.950
Since we're already here, let's browse in some of the shops.

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:55.780
Your dad did give you extra money. {lit: You got a tip}

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:56.550
Yeah, he did.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:58.770
Let's go, go!

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:00.800
Kukai?

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.890
Are you gonna buy that?

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:05.300
Yo, Hinamori.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.840
A present for Shion-san?

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:09.670
Yeah.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:11.350
I knew it was love!

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:13.110
I'm telling you, it's not.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:15.490
But you're looking for a present, right?

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:20.390
Well, it's more of a farewell gift than a birthday present.

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:23.840
A farewell gift? Even so, something like that's...

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:25.820
No good!

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:26.430
Really?

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:28.770
You are so completely clueless! {lit: taste}

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:33.210
But that Shion, she's kind of...

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:37.950
Even though she's going to chase her dream, she doesn't seem motivated.

00:10:38.090 --> 00:10:40.440
Oh, I see.

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:44.370
Utau.

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:47.660
I didn't announce today's performance.

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:53.220
We're going to see how big of an audience you can draw on your own {lit: using your own ability}

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:57.500
for the sake of our new strategy.

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:00.320
Strategy, huh?

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:04.540
Of course, if we find the Embryo, it's a different story.

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:10.350
You're on in thirty minutes. I'm expecting good results, Utau.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:17.860
I'll definitely get the Embryo myself.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:20.860
Yes, for Ikuto.

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:27.190
Who cares about that old broad?

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:30.240
Let's do what we want, Utau!

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:33.140
Yes, Il.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:48.920
I just can't decide, and you complained about everything! {lit: said, too much about everything}

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:51.790
That's because you only picked weird things.

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:53.850
Are you guys shopping together? {lit: chummily shopping}

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:55.580
Shion!

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:58.190
So she's the one you're serious about.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:05.480
N-No, I-I'm not! I mean, I was never interested in him in the first place!

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:08.010
Hinamori, why are you getting all worked up?

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:17.510
I won't get to see this view anymore. That's rather sad.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:21.480
You're racing toward your dream, right? Don't be so weak-spirited.

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:28.170
You know, doubt, uncertainty and dreams come in a set.

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:34.300
Looking for a four-leaf clover. I thought I might find one here.

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:39.750
Well then, I'll get out of your way. {lit: The intrusion will disappear}

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:42.630
You two kids have fun.

00:12:56.370 --> 00:12:57.890
Hey, this song...

00:12:57.930 --> 00:12:59.780
I think it's Utau-chan's.

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:01.590
Oh, look!

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:02.430
What?

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:06.020
Hoshina Utau!

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:12.600
Well then, shall we begin, Utau?

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:16.380
Let's hurry! I heard Utau-chan's here!

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:19.410
Utau? Hoshina Utau?

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:27.590
Wow.

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:34.980
Don't stare at me, don't capture me. {mitsumenaide...}

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:41.780
I'm a butterfly that's lost her way. {mayoikonda...}

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:48.440
I sing of freedom on invisible wings;  {jiyuu...}

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:56.180
I've hidden them deep inside your heart.{kakushiteru...}

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:09.380
The face reflected in the mirror {kagami...}

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:07.990
What's wrong, Daichi?

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:09.320
And you guys, too.

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:12.010
was nothing but a crybaby back then. {nakimushi...}

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:11.450
I sense the presence of an egg!

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:13.600
Lots of them all of a sudden.

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:15.500
But I'm no longer a child; {dakeredemo...}

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:15.190
They're giving me a bad feeling.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:17.110
Could they be X Eggs?

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:18.930
I've let down this long-grown hair. {nobashita...}

00:14:19.030 --> 00:14:25.710
Pressing the sweet fragrance close to my chest, {mune o...}

00:14:23.930 --> 00:14:25.680
Hinamori, I'll go ahead!

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:28.040
Wait up! You're too fast!

00:14:26.020 --> 00:14:32.300
its temptation makes me realize... {yuuwaku shiteru...}

00:14:35.380 --> 00:14:36.500
What is this?

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:41.200
Shion!

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:44.230
Hey, Shion!

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:46.510
Kukai.

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:49.140
Kukai, over there!

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:52.300
X Eggs. A ton of them!

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:57.260
They're all junk. I've no use for eggs that aren't the Embryo.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:00.770
Let's go, Daichi!

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:01.850
What about Shion?

00:15:01.890 --> 00:15:03.050
We'll come right back!

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:05.320
Amu-chan, over here!

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:07.060
R-Right.

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:11.790
Only authorized personnel are allowed back here.

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:24.020
Hoshina Utau?

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:26.820
Hinamori Amu.

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:30.440
What are you doing here?

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:32.650
Uh, um...

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:34.090
Amu-chan, look at that!

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:38.020
There are two Guardian Eggs.

00:15:38.070 --> 00:15:40.010
It looks like these two have already... {hatched}

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:42.240
Blah, blah, blah, blah, blah...

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.310
Shut up!

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.480
A Guardian Character?

00:15:49.690 --> 00:15:51.310
All right, they're all locked up!

00:15:51.710 --> 00:15:53.660
Now you can't get away.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:54.930
Let's go, Kukai!

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:55.680
Yeah.

00:15:56.480 --> 00:15:58.030
Character Change!

00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:06.250
Got one.

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:07.480
Nice catch.

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:11.110
All right, next!

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:15.080
That X Egg smells like Shion.

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:16.380
What do you mean?

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:19.730
That's definitely Shion's X Egg!

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:23.580
The way I play isn't good.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:26.580
Why did Shion's egg turn into an X Egg?

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:33.450
You know, doubt, uncertainty and dreams come in a set. {XXX Repeat of previous line}

00:16:35.540 --> 00:16:40.000
I'll definitely protect Shion's dream. Daichi!

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:41.060
Right!

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:49.190
Utau, are those guys Hinamori Amu's Guardian Characters?

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:50.800
That's right, Il.

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:58.490
None of them look like they amount to much.

00:16:58.920 --> 00:17:01.300
This Guardian Character has a pretty sharp tongue.

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:03.290
So you're a Character Bearer, too.

00:17:03.510 --> 00:17:08.960
What of it? Do you want to say that you're better than me because you have three?

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:10.370
No, of course not.

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:13.610
Amu-chan, the one we sensed was Il!

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:14.840
Oh, well then...

00:17:14.890 --> 00:17:18.090
But there were definitely X Eggs, too.

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:20.520
Yeah, we have to hurry and find them.

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:21.780
You're so stupid.

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:22.710
What?

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:27.390
Everyone gives up the eggs of who they want to be so easily. {"naritai jibun", like in OP1}

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:30.080
So to let it upset you, and to try so hard...

00:17:30.130 --> 00:17:31.780
Are you stupid?

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:35.370
It's not like that, and that's not what I think.

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:39.560
Besides, I decided...

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.480
I'd fix all the X Eggs! {XXX match the line in ep.13}

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:45.050
Whatever.

00:17:45.340 --> 00:17:46.640
We're going, Il.

00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:47.740
Gotcha.

00:17:49.310 --> 00:17:51.360
Amu-chan, we have to go, too!

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:52.520
Oh, yeah.

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:58.090
All right!

00:17:58.190 --> 00:18:00.620
Hey, quit struggling!

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:05.160
Just a few more.

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:07.380
Yeah, we just have to hold out a little longer.

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:09.500
Hinamori!

00:18:09.550 --> 00:18:11.060
I'm sorry I kept you waiting.

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:12.290
Miki, let's go.

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:13.070
Okay!

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:18.250
My heart: Unlock!

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:34.200
Character Transformation: Amulet Spade!

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:38.040
Amu-chan, gather all the X Eggs in one spot.

00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:39.050
Okay!

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:40.930
I'm counting on you, Hinamori!

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:44.050
Colorful Canvas!

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:48.100
This is a dead end!

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:50.630
Please go back the other way.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:53.790
Hinamori, take care of these, too!

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:54.830
You got it!

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:58.650
Once again, Colorful Canvas!

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:05.880
Negative Heart: Lock On!

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:11.120
Open Heart!

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:16.690
She got 'em!

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.990
That's our Joker! You're good!

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:29.440
It was a little tiring, though.

00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:37.260
Huh?

00:19:41.250 --> 00:19:49.520
Huh? What... What was that awful feeling?

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:52.840
It looks like they're all okay.

00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:53.830
Yeah.

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:56.200
That wraps it up.

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:57.600
All right!

00:19:57.650 --> 00:19:58.920
All right!

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:04.130
Jeez, what's Kukai doing?

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:06.820
To be late now, of all times! {he's the worst}

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.840
Maybe he had trouble deciding on a farewell gift.

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:10.700
That must be it.

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:12.100
Good grief.

00:20:14.550 --> 00:20:15.750
I have to go.

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:16.680
What?

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:18.030
Thanks for coming.

00:20:18.090 --> 00:20:18.590
But...

00:20:18.640 --> 00:20:19.540
Shion!

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:21.550
Kukai.

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:26.260
Sorry I'm late!

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:28.730
Here!

00:20:31.070 --> 00:20:32.350
Kukai.

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:35.570
A farewell gift and birthday present!

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:39.290
He was looking for a four-leaf clover!

00:20:39.330 --> 00:20:42.100
We had a really hard time finding one.

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:46.570
It's a good luck charm that should take care of{lit: blow off} your doubts and uncertainties.

00:20:47.070 --> 00:20:48.020
Yeah.

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:52.560
Nobody knows how far you can go.

00:20:52.690 --> 00:20:55.720
But that's what makes it exciting, right?

00:20:57.280 --> 00:21:00.840
After all, doesn't it mean you can go as far as you want?

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:04.680
Right.

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:15.650
Thanks.

00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:39.660
Well, she's gone.

00:21:41.560 --> 00:21:43.120
K-Kukai, what's wrong?

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.820
Could it have been love, after all?

00:21:45.890 --> 00:21:46.570
Huh?

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:48.020
He's back!

00:21:49.690 --> 00:21:51.900
Yeah, maybe.

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:55.660
Hinamori, it's been a while, so let's do that.

00:21:55.810 --> 00:21:56.810
Do what?

00:21:56.890 --> 00:21:58.340
Running dash! {XXX This should match whatever he called it back in ep 2 or 3 when they were doing their "special training"}

00:21:58.530 --> 00:22:00.030
Huh? Wait, hold on!

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:03.000
Why'd it turn out like this?

00:22:08.940 --> 00:22:12.590
That guy. He's going to be a good one.

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:41.890
Unless the world ends, I'll always {sekai ga...}

00:22:41.890 --> 00:22:44.660
love you!  Yeah, you! {suki da yo...}

00:22:44.660 --> 00:22:48.130
'Cause I just love, love, love you! {suki suki suki...}

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:52.860
Sure, I might struggle, but I'm still living. {jitabata...}

00:22:52.860 --> 00:22:55.540
So figure it out already! Yeah, you! {kizukeyo...}

00:22:55.540 --> 00:22:59.180
Even though I love, love, love you, {suki suki suki...}

00:22:59.880 --> 00:23:05.370
I wanna say it but, shoot, I just can't! {iitaikuseni...}

00:23:05.370 --> 00:23:09.490
I wanna show you what's in my heart! {tsutaetai...}

00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:12.920
Oh yes! You're my one true hero. {oh yes!...}

00:23:12.920 --> 00:23:18.080
Being in love's gonna be a bumpy ride.  {koishiterukagiri...}

00:23:18.080 --> 00:23:24.010
But keep going! Okay, greenhorn rider? {hashitsuzukero...}

00:23:24.010 --> 00:23:29.260
Straight down the path, into the sunset, stronger and stronger. {yuuyake...}

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:38.130
Ride through the wild land of youth. {seishun no...}

00:23:50.320 --> 00:23:52.980
I've got a strange feeling.  {lit: premonition}

00:23:53.010 --> 00:23:54.310
A strange feeling? What about?

00:23:54.350 --> 00:23:56.380
I feel like we're going to see him again.

00:23:56.440 --> 00:23:57.340
"Him?"

00:23:57.410 --> 00:24:00.100
Perhaps it's Miki's old boyfriend.

00:24:00.150 --> 00:24:02.190
No! You know, that guy with the glasses!

00:24:02.230 --> 00:24:03.570
You mean Nikaidou?

00:24:03.600 --> 00:24:04.330
Yoru!

00:24:04.380 --> 00:24:07.320
That guy's planning something-nya.

00:24:07.370 --> 00:24:08.580
Do you know something about it?

00:24:08.620 --> 00:24:09.920
I'm not telling! {lit: dunno}

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:12.650
Next time on Shugo Chara: Guardian Characters Kidnapped!

00:24:12.690 --> 00:24:14.310
Huh?! What do you mean by kidnapped?!

00:24:14.350 --> 00:24:15.430
What do we do? What do we do?

00:24:15.460 --> 00:24:16.470
This is terrible!

00:24:16.500 --> 00:24:17.880
Now, calm down-nya.

00:24:17.930 --> 00:24:19.790
How can we calm down?!
